[I] Lightweight replacement for GNU autotools written for bmake

[T] mk-configure is a build system written in and for bmake and UNIX tools.
[T] It provides mk include files for building executables and libraries,
[T] autoconf like feature checks and the mkcmake wrapper, used for example by
[T] libmaa.

[U] https://github.com/cheusov/mk-configure

[A] Aleksey Cheusov <vle@gmx.net>
[M] The T2 Project <t2@t2-project.org>

[C] extra/development
[F] CROSS

[L] BSD
[V] 0.40.3
[P] X -----5---9 120.100

[D] 8a8718259b5235285035613cc94119e11ab4324c56a65d1ba7671a7b mk-configure-0.40.3.tar.gz https://github.com/cheusov/mk-configure/archive/mk-configure-0.40.3/

runconf=0 runmake=0

export PREFIX=/$prefix SYSCONFDIR=$sysconfdir MANDIR=$mandir DOCDIR=$docdir

hook_add premake 5 "bmake all"
hook_add inmake 5 "bmake installdirs install DESTDIR=$root"
